- [high] internal/service/worker/service.go:331 (correctness vs. the actual SDK/library): The dashboard suggestion worker is registered through river.WorkFunc, whose wrapper embeds River WorkerDefaults and does not consult DashboardSuggestionCellArgs.Timeout(). In River v0.30 the timeout must come from the Worker Timeout method or river.Config.JobTimeout, so this job inherits River default JobTimeout (1 minute) instead of the intended 5 minutes. That is shorter than the default AI request timeout (120s), and completeWithOneRetry can make two such calls, so normal slow LLM calls can be cancelled by River before the worker request timeout/retry policy completes; on the final attempt the failure-marking path then uses the cancelled job context and can leave the cell pending while River discards the job.
